New Era)\", which became their first number one single in South Korea. It won Song of the Year at the SPOTV K-pop Awards and was nominated for the Grammy Award for Best Asian Pop Music Performance.","title":"Leesol","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leesol"}},"Q16084047":{"id":"Q16084047","name":"Jo Seung-hee","ko":"조승희","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Cho Yi-hyeon"],"birth":"1991-06-03","death":"","birthplace":"Gwangju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","model"],"debut":"2013","agencies":[{"name":"MBK Entertainment","id":"Q429296","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q486683","name":"F-ve Dolls","start":"2013","end":"2015"},{"id":"Q20733515","name":"DIA","start":"2015","end":"2016"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/seunghee91_63/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/46792d86-8639-475f-a32e-41eaac70d5bb"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Cho Seung-hee, better known as Cho Yi-hyun (조이현), is a South Korean actress, singer, general producer of the label company PocketDol Studio and founder of PocketDol Studio's label M25. She debuted as new member of F-ve Dolls in 2013 and continued to promote until the group unofficially disbanded in November 2014, which was confirmed in March 2015. Following the disbandment, she returned as a trainee for almost a year before re-debuting as the leader of DIA in September 2015. In April 2016, she left DIA after her contract expired to pursue her acting career. She has established herself as an actress with cast in various television dramas such as Mr.","title":"Cho Seung-hee","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cho_Seung-hee"}},"Q16767951":{"id":"Q16767951","name":"Hani","ko":"안희연","birthName":"안희연","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Ahn Hee-yeon"],"birth":"1992-05-01","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","presenter","model","film actor"],"debut":"2012","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q492381","name":"EXID","start":"2012","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/ahnhani_92/","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@hanixheeyeon","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/d0b1d8ef-fe57-4c10-b467-41caf43646be"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Ahn Hee-yeon, known professionally as Hani (하니), is a South Korean singer and actress. She is known as a member of the South Korean girl group EXID and its subgroup, SoljiHani (formerly known as Dasoni (다소니)). She has appeared on television as a host on Weekly Idol and a cast member on Off to School, Crime Scene and A Style for You.","title":"Hani (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hani_%28singer%29"}},"Q17403471":{"id":"Q17403471","name":"Subin","ko":"수빈","birthName":"박수빈","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Park Su-bin","DJ Suvin","DALsooobin","SUVIN"],"birth":"1994-02-12","death":"","birthplace":"Gwangju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","model","songwriter","disc jockey"],"debut":"2011","agencies":[{"name":"Happy Face Entertainment","id":"Q15154003","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q492146","name":"Dal Shabet","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/dalsooobin/","x":"https://x.com/dal_sooobin","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCNBqgJYMhqRm9HFvl2a3fzw","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0ZjVwJw2cFymrcIwmGuVEl","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/f052cfd8-205f-42d7-a501-53c54c30ac95"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Park Subin, better known as Subin or Dalsooobin or her DJ name SUVIN, is a South Korean singer, songwriter, actress, television host, and DJ. She made her debut in 2011 as a member of the South Korean girl group Dal Shabet. She made her solo debut in 2016.","title":"Park Subin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park_Subin"}},"Q18550351":{"id":"Q18550351","name":"Kim Jin-hwan","ko":"김진환","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Jay"],"birth":"1994-02-07","death":"","birthplace":"Jeju","natio