record producer. On March 25, 2016, he released his debut EP, 130 Mood: TRBL, and multiple collaborations with American and South Korean artists. In 2017, he appeared as one of the producers on the South Korean rap competition TV show Show Me the Money 6 with Zico. He is part of the hip hop crew Fanxy Child with fellow singers Zico, Crush, Penomeco, Millic, and Stay Tuned.","title":"Dean (South Korean singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dean_%28South_Korean_singer%29"}},"Q24836815":{"id":"Q24836815","name":"Casper True","ko":"캐스퍼","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Casper Chu","C. True","Chu Xiaoxiang"],"birth":"1991-03-20","death":"","birthplace":"Shanghai","nationality":["People's Republic of China"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","songwriter","composer","record producer","actor"],"debut":"2009","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q307621","name":"Cross Gene","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/casper.true/","x":"https://x.com/caspertrue1991","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCYaAnVmpiaw_SXfHLMEJSig","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Kk0sn6k9Q4mNT2xUq7Erz","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/24d93b45-d6fb-44fd-9a7f-95f9edaa74a9"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q26451151":{"id":"Q26451151","name":"Ten","ko":"텐 (가수)","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Chittaphon Leechaiyapornkul","Ten Lee"],"birth":"1996-02-27","death":"","birthplace":"Bangkok","nationality":["Thailand"],"height":172,"occupations":["singer","dancer","fashion designer","rapper"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Capitol Records","id":"Q193023","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q66710876","name":"SuperM","start":"2019","end":"2021"},{"id":"Q23725822","name":"NCT","start":"","end":""},{"id":"Q67972645","name":"NCT U","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/tenlee_1001/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/135a6e96-6a29-4999-a18c-06b0c38b0e7b"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Chittaphon Leechaiyapornkul, known professionally as Ten, is a Thai singer and dancer. He debuted with the South Korean boy band under SM Entertainment, NCT, in 2016 as part of its first sub-unit, NCT U. Since 2019, he has been active mainly as a member of NCT's China-based unit WayV and the South Korean supergroup SuperM. Ten has also released several solo singles through the SM Station project: \"Dream in a Dream\" (2017), \"New Heroes\" (2018), \"Paint Me Naked\" (2021), and \"Birthday\" (2022). He made his solo debut in February 2024 with his eponymous extended play.","title":"Ten (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ten_%28singer%29"}},"Q26707663":{"id":"Q26707663","name":"Lisa","ko":"리사","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lalisa Manobal","Lisa Manobal","Pranpriya Manobal","Lalisa Manoban"],"birth":"1997-03-27","death":"","birthplace":"Buri Ram","nationality":["Thailand"],"height":168,"occupations":["singer-songwriter","dancer","model","rapper","songwriter","fashion model"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"YG Entertainment","id":"Q50595","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Interscope Records","id":"Q231694","start":"","end":""},{"name":"LLOUD","id":"Q124485291","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q25056945","name":"Blackpink","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"website":"https://www.lalisaofficial.com/","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/lalalalisa_m/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC35HKvKYPkri4Grd5KXl3wQ","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@lalalalisa_m","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5L1lO4eRHmJ7a0Q6csE5cT","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/30aeb57f-bb16-47fa-86ca-79fc57b4d12c"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lalisa Manobal, known mononymously as Lisa, is a Thai rapper, singer, dancer, and actress. She rose to prominence as a member of the South Korean girl group Blackpink, which debuted under YG Entertainment in August 2016 and became one of the best-selling girl groups of all time. In September 2021, Lisa released her debut single album Lalisa, which made her the first female artist to sell 736,000 copies of an album in its first week in South Korea and spawned the Billboard Global 200 top-ten singles \"Lalisa\" and \"Money\".","title":"Lisa (rapper)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisa_%28rapper%29"}},"Q30923727":{"id":"Q30923727","name":"Lee So-yul","ko":"이소율","birthName":"이소율","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Jenny","Jenny"],"birth":"1996-09-14","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","musician","actor"],"debut":"","agencies":[{"name":"MBK Entertainment","id":"Q429296","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20733515","name":"DIA","start":"2015","end":"2019"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/yulleda/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/a2154909-6280-47e4-a1bc-0f1b0c52f4f9"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q31179151":{"id":"Q31179151","name":"Babylon","ko":"베이빌론","birthName":"이종민","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1988","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2011","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q486808","name":"N-Train","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/thebabylon/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/270bf8e5-6254-46e5-ac7e-20391c93ef38"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/%28Marie_Claire_Korea%29_%EB%A7%88%EB%A6%AC%ED%94%8C%EB%A0%88%EC%9D%B4%EB%A6%AC%EC%8A%A4%ED%8A%B8_%EB%B2%A0%EC%9D%B4%EB%B9%8C%EB%A1%A0_%ED%8E%B8_15s.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Marie_Claire_Korea)_%EB%A7%88%EB%A6%AC%ED%94%8C%EB%A0%88%EC%9D%B4%EB%A6%AC%EC%8A%A4%ED%8A%B8_%EB%B2%A0%EC%9D%B4%EB%B9%8C%EB%A1%A0_%ED%8E%B8_15s.JPG","author":"Marie Claire Korea","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Lee Jong-min, better known by his stage name Babylon (베이빌론), is a South Korean singer-songwriter, rapper, and dancer. He debuted as an idol in the five-member group N-Train under Media Line Entertainment, where he served as a vocalist from 2011 to its dissolution in 2013. He debuted as a soloist in 2015 with \"Pray\" and released his debut studio album Caelo in 2018.","title":"Babylon (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babylon_%28singer%29"}},"Q484815":{"id":"Q484815","name":"Jun. K","ko":"","birthName":"김민준","birthNameEn":"Kim Min-jun","aliases":["Kim Min-jun","Kim Jun-su","Jun Ke-i","Jun Kei","Gim Min-jun","Kim Minchun"],"birth":"1988-01-15","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["rapper","actor","singer","record producer","songwriter","lyricist"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q222760","name":"2PM","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jun2dakay/","x":"https://x.com/Jun2daKAY","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/da183054-32a1-421c-9df3-ee31f158ee33"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Min-jun, known professionally as Jun. K (준케이), is a South Korean singer-songwriter, rapper, record producer, and actor. He is the main vocalist of 2PM, a boy band currently managed by JYP Entertainment, and he has written and composed several of the group's songs, including \"Go Crazy!\", \"My House\", and \"With Me Again\". Formerly known as Kim Jun-su, he revealed on October 17, 2012, that due to family reasons, he would be changing his name to Min-jun, though his stage name would remain the same. Aside from his group activities, Jun. K has released five EPs in South Korea and six EPs and one compilation album in Japan.","title":"Jun. K","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jun._K"}},"Q489103":{"id":"Q489103","name":"Brian Joo","ko":"브라이언","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","alias